[36m(TaskRunner pid=107890)[0m We need \( b + 7 \) to be a divisor of \( 9b + 7 \). This can be expressed as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=107890)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=107890)[0m where \( k \) is a positive integer.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=107890)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=107890)[0m Rewriting the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=107890)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=107890)[0m Expanding and rearranging terms:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=107890)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = kb + 7k \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=107890)[0m \[ 9b - kb + 7 - 7k = 0 \]
